{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/90659-on-changeling-bodies","id":90659,"title":"On Changeling Bodies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-13T21:59:25-07:00","id":90659,"title":"On Changeling Bodies","content":"When captured by the Fae, changelings' bodies can be radically altered, even to the point of becoming non-mammalian forms of life or base matter (ice, stone, clockwork parts, etc.). This is to say nothing of anatomical impossibilities, like the changeling whose Keeper <i>literally</i> stole his heart.<br /> <br /> Now as far as perception goes, the Mask covers all this quite well, but what happens when these physical transformations meet with equally physical forces? Do poisons deadly to humans (or mammals in general) have the same effects on lizard-men or spider-women? If a hollow man stuffed with straw has a limb cut off, does he still have to worry about bleeding out? And what happens when a vampire tries to snack on a literal ice maiden?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-13T22:21:43-07:00","id":90666,"title":"","content":"The mien of the Lost is mostly metaphorical imagery that functions like human physiology - a Stonebones isn't any more durable that a Gristlegrinder without spending Glamour, and a Snowskin's tendency to melt slightly in higher temperatures isn't going to manifest as taking damage significantly sooner than a mortal unless they're afflicted with a frailty to that effect.<br /> <br /> At higher Wyrd or in the case of the Fae themselves, of course, most if not all bets are off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T08:44:22-07:00","id":90922,"title":"","content":"What Satchel said. As Wyrd grows, sometimes aspects of the Mien become less metaphorical and a bit more concrete, though it's not guaranteed. The merit I was working on, Faerie Form, was meant to represent some of the more outr\u00e9 changes to a 'ling bod. I really need to get up the gumption to finalize it.<br /> <br /> Equinox Road has some stuff on changeling Miens that might be relevant to your questions. Rites of Spring too, I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T19:21:20-07:00","id":92571,"title":"","content":"Personally. I think they should have been a little bit more like Wyld mutants from exalted with base advantages and deformities in a package but it's not the kind of system that works in Changeling. Assume the form is just a minor physical change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T07:25:06-07:00","id":95600,"title":"","content":"Given that even a single dot of Wyrd is strong magic.... at what point do you start to allow some PC narrative benefits to increased Wyrd of form?<br /> <br /> Feathers that shed water<br /> Fur that buffers from wind<br /> Metal that defeats scratches","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}